kdeconnect (25.12.3-0supralinux8) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Apply plugin enable/disable settings immediately in the KDE Connect app.
    The app wrote the per-device configuration file but did not notify
    kdeconnectd, which keeps the plugin map in memory. Unticking "Receive
    notifications" therefore only took effect after a reconnect or daemon
    restart. Call Device::setPluginEnabled() over D-Bus so the daemon reloads
    the plugin map immediately.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:44:27 -0300

kdeconnect (25.12.3-0supralinux7) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Bluetooth: skip creating the Bluetooth link provider entirely when
    /sys/class/bluetooth does not exist. This also avoids the one-time
    QBluetooth/BlueZ initialization at daemon startup on machines without
    an adapter; the 0supralinux6 guards remain for the provider itself.
    Machines with an adapter keep the same behavior.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 06:55:00 -0300

kdeconnect (25.12.3-0supralinux6) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Bluetooth: do not query BlueZ when the system has no Bluetooth
    adapter. The link provider used to request org.bluez every 30 seconds
    through QBluetoothLocalDevice and wait for the 25-second D-Bus
    activation timeout. Check /sys/class/bluetooth on Linux and create the
    service discovery agent lazily, so machines without an adapter stay
    quiet while machines with one keep working.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 06:40:00 -0300

kdeconnect (25.12.3-0supralinux5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Virtual Monitor: launch krdc directly instead of KIO::OpenUrlJob.
    KIO treats the rdp:// URL as a remote file and fails with
    "Could not read file", so KRDC never started. Pass the URL, which
    already contains the one-time credentials, to the krdc binary.
    Also write the requested resolution to the global KRDC RDP group.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 01:15:00 -0300

kdeconnect (25.12.3-0supralinux4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Virtual Monitor: seed KRDC's FreeRDP certificate store with the KDE
    Connect certificate, configure TLS-only RDP, skip the first-connection
    settings dialog, and pass the client resolution. A paired SupraLINUX
    device opens the virtual monitor with a single click.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 01:00:00 -0300

kdeconnect (25.12.3-0supralinux3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Pass the KDE Connect TLS certificate and key to krdpserver so the
    Virtual Monitor server starts on a fresh profile.
  * Launch the remote RDP client through KIO instead of relying on
    xdg-open/kfmclient, which is not available in the Plasma 6 session.
  * Link the virtualmonitor plugin with KIOWidgets and Notifications.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 02:40:00 -0300

kdeconnect (25.12.3-0supralinux2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add the native SFTP server side to the sftp plugin.  A paired Linux
    device can now answer kdeconnect.sftp.request by launching
    supralinux-kdeconnect-sftp, an ephemeral per-user server authenticated
    with the paired device certificate.  No system sshd, port 22, ~/.ssh or
    known_hosts changes are involved.
  * Use physical pixels for Virtual Monitor capabilities on HiDPI screens
    (upstream fix present in 26.04.3).

